[{"category":"section","location":"literate/io/","page":"Save / load","text":"using LocalStore\n\nDefine an item type. This should contain enough information to be able to reconstruct the desired object.\n\nstruct A\n    x::Int\nend\n\nSince store location is based on hash, it is recommended to define a hash function for custom types.\n\nBase.hash(a::A, h::UInt) = hash(:A, hash(a.x, h))\n\nDefine how the item is stored on disk. The path is a dir, handled automatically by the LocalStore package.\n\nLocalStore.save(a::A, path::String) = open(\"$path/file.txt\", \"w\") do f\n    # some difficult computation you only want to do once\n    x2 = a.x^2\n    # maybe download some remote files\n\n    # now save to disk the results\n    write(f, string(x2))\nend\n\nDefine how the item is read from disk.\n\nLocalStore.load(a::A, path::String) = open(\"$path/file.txt\", \"r\") do f\n    parse(Int, readline(f))\nend\n\nAutomatically checks if the requested object is stored. If not, it creates a local directory and saves it there and loads it. Next time load is called, the stored object is returned.\n\na = LocalStore.load(A(5))\n\n\n\nThis page was generated using Literate.jl.","title":"Save / load"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/#Reference","page":"Reference","text":"","title":"Reference"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#LocalStore.clean-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"clean(obj)\n\nRemoves the stored data associated with obj.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LocalStore.clean"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#LocalStore.clean-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"clean(; force=false)\n\nRemoves all stored data directories.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LocalStore.clean"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#LocalStore.expected_tree_hash-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"expected_tree_hash(obj)\n\nExpected tree hash for the saved contents of obj. Overload this for specific item types. Otherwise simply returns the hash of the contents of the store (so no verification happens).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LocalStore.expected_tree_hash"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#LocalStore.issaved-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"issaved(obj)\n\nReturns true if obj is locally stored, false otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LocalStore.issaved"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#LocalStore.itemdir-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"itemdir(obj)\n\nDirectory path where obj will be stored.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LocalStore.itemdir"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#LocalStore.load-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"load(obj)\n\nReads and returns the specified object. Stores it locally if it hasn't been stored already.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LocalStore.load"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#LocalStore.rootdir-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"rootdir()\n\nRoot directory path where objects will be stored.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LocalStore.rootdir"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#LocalStore.save-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"save(obj)\n\nStores obj locally if it has not been stored already. Returns path to directory containing obj.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LocalStore.save"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#LocalStore.verify-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"verify(obj)\n\nCompares the treehash of the stored copy of obj to the expected treehash, and errors if there is a difference.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LocalStore.verify"},{"category":"section","location":"#LocalStore.jl-Documentation","page":"Home","text":"A Julia package that provides a simple interface for storing and retrieving Julia objects locally.","title":"LocalStore.jl Documentation"}]
